The issue desk is built under `src/`: three pages behind the tabs, with each page's state and server requests in XState v5 machines, and the open-issue count kept at app level. `./check` passes and all 30 visible tests pass (6 of 15 runs used). I also ran the decline paths and the help and settings edge cases through a scratch Node simulation (`scratch/sim2.ts`), which matched the brief; I'm unsure of three things: the detail assign error reads `assign error: declined` (the brief only says "the server's message"), the browser logs one 404 during the first test, and I did not trim the settings name when saving.

Files are in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/desk9-xstate-haiku-6/src/`: `App.tsx`, `machines/{app,issues,help,settings,ops}.ts`, and `pages/{IssuesPage,HelpPage,SettingsPage}.tsx`.